[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. The reports in it say otherwise:
#4471 holds three problems. Each now has its own ticket.

| problem | ticket |
|---|---|
| `parser`: the shared parser reads day-first dates month first | [#5](https://github.com/adrianoresende/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/5) |
| `hint`: booking-v3 hints `MM/DD/YYYY` to day-first tenants | [#2](https://github.com/adrianoresende/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/2) |
| one-day move: invites land one day off (time zone), not a day/month flip | [#3](https://github.com/adrianoresende/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/3) |

<Callout kind="warn">
Shipping the parser fix closes the biggest group only. The other two keep coming in.
</Callout>

## How many reports each covers

Counted by the desk's own view: one id per report, placed by tenant (`causes.ts`), not by
intake's tag. The one-day moves are the reports the desk already read that way (desk-notes);
they stay counted where they are filed, under `parser`, and are the whole of ticket #3.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

1. **`parser` ([#5](https://github.com/adrianoresende/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/5)).** The shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first
   tenant's `5/3` becomes 3 May. This is the fix that is queued.
2. **`hint` ([#2](https://github.com/adrianoresende/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/2)).** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at
   day-first tenants on booking-v3 type what the hint says, and the form reads it the tenant's
   way. Only reports that came in through the form. The parser fix does not touch it. Today it
   has no ticket of its own: the table above marks it in red.
3. **One-day move ([#3](https://github.com/adrianoresende/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/3)).** "Tuesday 12 May, calendar says Monday 11 May"; "Lisbon got
   Tuesday, Toronto got Monday"; "the invite arrived before I made the booking". No day and
   month swap explains these. It is a time-zone or DST conversion bug, not the parser.

## What changes on the desk

- Matching on subject (decision 0001) merged these: the same subjects came in for all three
  problems. Splitting needs the tenant and the body, not the subject.
- Close #4471 against the `parser` ticket only, and keep the other two open after the fix ships.

